; Alice pays while flag is false, flag becomes true at entry 2, Alice refunds,
; then Bob leaks. In the first term the payment at entry 1 completes the first
; part, so a reading of that prefix has reached the prohibition, and only a
; violation can end the observation: the refund at entry 3 completes the
; interrupted reading but does not end it, and the leak is a violation at
; entry 4 (formal/core/CORE.md, decision 34). In the second term the payment
; completes the term at entry 1 before any reading reaches the prohibition of
; the handler, so its status is DONE at entry 1, although the whole trace is a
; violated trace in the reading where the guard interrupts the obligation: a
; violation is missed only after such a completion. In the third and the
; fourth term a branch of OR is a prohibition, and the leak is a violation.
(scenario readings_guard_after_pay
  (spec "examples/core/core_readings.triel")
  (entry "2026-06-01T00:00:00Z" (activate)
    (data (flag (bool false))))
  (entry "2026-06-01T01:00:00Z" (act alice pay must)
    (data (flag (bool false))))
  (entry "2026-06-01T02:00:00Z" (tick)
    (data (flag (bool true))))
  (entry "2026-06-01T03:00:00Z" (act alice refund must)
    (data (flag (bool true))))
  (entry "2026-06-01T04:00:00Z" (act bob leak must_not)
    (data (flag (bool true)))))
